joining us right now fresh off  dominating another olympics  katie ledecky joins the show the  three-time olympian the seven-time gold  medalist congratulations katie on  another  incredible run in tokyo my first  question do you  check the metals do you fly with them  carry on how do the metals get back home  yeah hi ben um yeah i flew with them and  my  in my carry-on they're they're safe and  sound and um  still still looking as good as when i  got them we talk a lot around the nfl  when these guys get their super bowl  rings of where they wear their rings  if they're just going to whole foods  picking up some groceries now let me  just pull out the super bowl ring  where do you wear gold medals  uh well i do keep them nearby the the  first couple weeks and months because a  lot of people do  do like to see them um i i wouldn't say  i take them to the grocery store on a  regular basis  but hey you know sometimes sometimes  there's somebody there that wants to see  it so  i'll bring it by katie ledecky joins the  show she's partnered with bic  razors for the game on campaign which is  about the importance of having  self-confidence and  katie what big takeaway from this  olympics of course is i think for the  rest  of us civilians we've finally been let  into  the thought process of what it means to  be a professional athlete and the impact  that has  on your confidence and on your  self-esteem so talk to me a little bit  about  this issue that's facing not only your  sport the olympics but just  sports and humanity in general the idea  of taking care of our mental health  yeah i think you know what i'll say is  i'm so grateful for the opportunity that  represented team usa and i'm  really proud of all my team team usa  teammates for  what they've done on the field in the  pool in the gym  but also what they've done off of it and  while the medals and the records  that i've achieved at this this  competition are  a validation for all the hard work that  i've put in over the  past several years my my primary goal  was  was to leave tokyo having inspired  others and  that's really been at the heart of my  partnership with with vic and  and big soleil razors uh we want to  inspire people to be confident when  they're  they're chasing their dreams then not be  afraid to show it um  and i'm uh really happy with with how my  my meat went in tokyo and i'm really  happy with with all the experiences i  had and  i felt like i was was confident behind  the blocks and and felt really good  about  each one of my races and i hope that all  of my teammates and i inspired  a lot of a lot of swimmers out there a  lot of young kids to dream big and  not be afraid to work really hard to  achieve big things  whether that's in the pool or out of the  pool or in some other sport or  in school or whatever it is that that  you're passionate about  because i think if you you have some big  goals you have some confidence  and you believe in yourself you can do  some big things  katie ledecky joins the show seven-time  gold medalist three-time olympian ben  lion's in for rich the rich eisen show  katie when tj jefferson wins one week of  fantasy football  he's on one all week he's celebrating  popping popping bottles he wins week  five  we don't see him till thursday what do  you do to celebrate  what's the turn up like now that you're  home  hey you know i i've had my share of  fancy football experiences like that as  well  um but you know it's um it's  i'm just trying to relax and enjoy this  and enjoy being with my family and  friends  being being reunited with with my family  and friends um  coming off these games and um just just  trying to let it all sink in  after the rio games i took a very short  two or three week break and i was  back at it with with my goals for tokyo  and  i do have my eyes set on on paris in  2024 and i know that i'll be  be back in the pool pretty soon uh  working hard for that but uh for right  now i'm  i'm really going to take a breather  enjoy being with my family and friends  and let it all soak in let's just take a  moment now round of applause  for it again because that was something  everybody in here was curious about the  idea of  is she gonna get back in the pool and  try and make another run out yeah katie  and you kind of gave michelle tafoya  some side eye when she suggested that  maybe  this was your last olympics when did you  make that decision and when are you  gonna start training again for paris  no you know i mean it was it was a  totally valid question and  i love michelle and i feel bad if uh  anyone thought that i  um had a reaction to that question at  all because  um no i've always had my my eyes set on  on paris and i think i've been pretty  clear about that  over the past several years and um i  i don't have my goals yet for paris all  i know is i want to be there and i want  to compete for team usa  and in the next several months i'll  start getting into the weeds in terms of  deciding what events i want to target  what kinds of times i want to achieve  um what kinds of metals i might want to  earn those kinds of things  but for right now i'm i'm keeping my  mind off of that as best i can  it's a little a little hard because yes  you do you do get asked that  um right after after the races from  anyone and everyone so um i know it's  gonna start becoming more and more of a  focus for me  over the next several months but for  right now as i said i'm still  still letting tokyo 2021 sink in  in addition to winning a ton of olympic  medals you mentioned that you've won  some weeks in fantasy football so katie  i'm very curious about your fantasy  approach  do you work the waiver wire do you try  and make a blockbuster trade  how do you construct your roster for  fantasy  you know i've been playing fantasy  football um with my  cousins for a while now and uh  some people are a little more serious  than others and i joke with my mom i  think  we're the two that probably do the most  adding and dropping of players  and some of my cousins who don't do  anything end up winning  more games than than we do so i think my  strategy going into this fall  is probably just gonna be to to be hands  off as much as possible and maybe even  have some uh  some some spots empty on my starting  roster like some of my cousins  do some weeks and see if that went  hey hey katie this is tj i want to say  congratulations  um and since i'm putting together a rich  eisen show fantasy football league i  would love to extend and invite to you  to play in our league what do you think  i mean you don't have to be here we're  pretty lacks  but you know we do expect you to put a  starting lineup in every every week so  um  the invite's there it's all i'm saying  okay  yeah i maybe created some some trouble  for myself  [Laughter]  got all sorts of invitations now well  this is what happens when you win a  bunch of meadows you get all types of  pitches and people want to do business  or they want to invite you in their  fantasy footballs  it's more so that we could say we have a  gold medalist yeah  in our league so it's it's more for us  than it is for you katie just to be  honest but we'd love to have you there  you uh you talked about inspiring the  next generation of swimmers or just  folks out there who are looking for that  inspiration  and you look at the performances that  not only you had out there  in tokyo but your teammates uh the  entire united states  swimming program the men and the women  what do you think  uh is the impact of going out there on  the olympic stage how have you seen that  inspiration be received in your own life  it's been awesome and i i had so much  fun with with my teammates  we were together for the four or five  weeks in between  olympic trials and and the olympics and  just had so much fun together and  it's it's more than the medals and the  records it's those memories  and and those times that you spend with  y